<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Verified against Android's own network security config docs before writing
  this (developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/security-config): the
  <domain> element only matches exact hostnames/IP literals, NOT CIDR ranges —
  an earlier draft of this file tried "192.168.0.0/16" as a <domain>, which
  would silently never match and leave cleartext blocked on a real device.
  Corrected to a base-config instead.

  Why base-config at all: SAM Core (desktop) is reached over plain HTTP on the
  local network today, not HTTPS — see docs/iqoo/PROTOCOL.md / OFFICE_KIT.md
  in the main repo ("same-WiFi HTTP"). The host is whatever IP the user enters
  during pairing (not known at build time), so a per-domain allowlist isn't
  possible here. This app makes no other network calls, so app-wide cleartext
  is the honest scope, not a wider hole than it looks.

  Revisit once Agent 3's real transport/pairing design lands — it may fix the
  host to an mDNS .local name (which COULD move this to a scoped domain-config)
  or add TLS outright.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
